+## Tag & Slug governance (the Hub spreadsheet)
+
+Several fields across the three sheets are deliberately closed to free
+text, to avoid a typo silently breaking a link or fragmenting a
+category (e.g. one project saying "European" and another "Europe").
+This is governed by a fourth, separate Google Sheet — the **Tag & Slug
+Hub** — plus a small Apps Script trigger in each of the three main
+spreadsheets.
+
+**The Hub has 8 tabs.** Director-edited word lists (single source of
+truth, edited only by whoever owns each list — today, Prof. Angelini):
+- `Funding Regions` — used by Projects, multi-select
+- `Project Status` — used by Projects
+- `Member Rank` — used by Members
+- `Activity Section` — used by Member Activities
+- `Publication Type` — used by Publications
+
+Auto-mirrored — nobody edits these directly, see "Slug auto-generation" below:
+- `Member Slugs`, `Project Slugs`, `Publication Slugs`
+
+**How a value gets from the Hub into a dropdown — two `IMPORTRANGE`
+hops, not one.** Data Validation can only pull from a range in the
+*same* spreadsheet file, so:
+1. Each of the 3 main spreadsheets has a hidden `_TagRef` tab that
+   mirrors the relevant Hub tab(s) via `IMPORTRANGE`.
+2. The actual column (e.g. Members' Rank column) has Data Validation
+   ("Dropdown from a range") pointing at that local `_TagRef` tab, not
+   at the Hub directly.
+3. Slugs flow the other way first: Members/Projects/Publications each
+   generate their own slug locally (see "Slug auto-generation"), the
+   Hub mirrors those into its own `Member Slugs`/`Project Slugs`/
+   `Publication Slugs` tabs, and *those* get mirrored back out to
+   whichever sheet needs to link to them — e.g. Publications'
+   `_TagRef` tab pulls both Member Slugs and Project Slugs from the Hub.
+
+IMPORTRANGE needs a one-time "Allow access" click (by anyone with edit
+rights on the destination and at least view rights on the source) the
+first time each pair of sheets is connected. After that it's automatic
+for everyone with access to the destination sheet — they never need
+direct access to the Hub itself.
+
+Adding a new allowed value (e.g. a new Funding Region) means adding one
+row to the relevant Hub tab, nothing else — it propagates on its own.
+
+## Slug auto-generation
+
+`Slug` columns (Members, Projects, Publications) are never typed by
+hand. Each of those three spreadsheets has an Apps Script `onEdit`
+trigger (Extensions → Apps Script, inside that spreadsheet) that:
+
+- Watches the Name/Title column. The moment it's filled in, it writes
+  a slugified version into the Slug column — but only if Slug is
+  still empty. Once set, it is never recalculated again, even if the
+  Name/Title changes later, which protects existing links from
+  Publications/Member Activities that already point at that slug.
+- Separately watches the Slug column itself: if someone directly
+  overwrites an existing (non-blank) slug, it shows a warning
+  explaining that anything already linking to the old slug will break.
+- (Members only) also watches Rank: the moment Rank is chosen, if
+  Role is still empty, it fills Role with a sensible default for that
+  rank (e.g. "PhD Candidate") — editable afterwards, and once Role has
+  any value it's never auto-overwritten again.
+
+**These scripts live only inside each spreadsheet's own Apps Script
+editor — they are not deployed from this repo, and Google Sheets keeps
+no version history for them.** Reference copies are kept in
+`apps-script/` in this repo purely so the logic survives if a script
+project is ever accidentally cleared. If you change a live script,
+copy the final version back into the matching file here so the two
+don't drift apart — see `apps-script/README.md`.
+
+**Why an Apps Script trigger instead of a plain spreadsheet formula:**
+an earlier version tried a self-referencing formula
+(`=IF(B2="",SLUGIFY(A2),B2)` with iterative calculation turned on) to
+get the same "compute once, then freeze" behavior without any script.
+Two real Google Sheets quirks broke it: calling a custom Apps Script
+function from inside a circular-reference formula can hang
+indefinitely on "Loading data…", and a fresh circular reference's very
+first evaluation treats the cell as numeric `0` rather than empty,
+which broke the "still empty" check. The `onEdit` trigger sidesteps
+both issues entirely.
